    "rationale": "Deterministic constraints (CPU-only, 4 GB RAM, max runtime memory 500 MB, max CPU latency 200 ms) favor the smallest-feasible architecture that can reliably hit the target accuracy on MNIST. Mobilenet_v3_small is the most compact model in the provided candidate set that still offers competitive accuracy for simple, grayscale, low-resolution data like MNIST. It has a low parameter count and lightweight operations, which translate to low memory usage and fast CPU inference, making it well-suited for a CPU-only system with the specified limits. While larger architectures could potentially yield marginally higher accuracy on more complex tasks, they risk breaching the latency/memory budgets here. Typical improvements to meet or exceed the 90% target on MNIST can be achieved with standard training practices and lightweight data augmentation, plus optional post-training quantization to further reduce runtime memory if needed. Trade-offs include slightly longer training time and the need to ensure the training setup emphasizes proper convergence on MNIST to reliably reach the target accuracy on the constrained device.",
