    "rationale": "Selection targets a lightweight, balanced per-class pool from a single coherent dataset family (MNIST training splits) to meet CPU and memory constraints while achieving the requested accuracy. For each digit (0\u20139), we pick mnist_cls_train with a pool of 1,500 images per class to hit the ~1.5k-per-class target and keep total volume within the recommended budget. This ensures domain alignment (handwritten grayscale digits) and stable class balance without mixing incompatible sources. Using only the training split adheres to the rule of including at least one train source and allows the final holdouts (validation and test) to be derived proportionally from each selected training pool. Expected derived holdout per class (assuming a common 70/15/15 split) is about 1,050 training, 225 validation, and 225 test images per class, i.e., roughly 450 images per class reserved for holdouts and about 1.05k per class for training. Across all 10 digits, this yields a ~15,000-image per-class total pool and ~4,500 holdout images, with an overall download volume well within the 50,000-image ceiling. The default download budget was not a limiting factor in this selection. If you want to adjust the per-class pool size (e.g., 1,200 or 2,000), I can re-tune accordingly.",
